   "slot": "member1_opening",
   "text": "A price crash for LUSD triggers the Stability Pool and debt redistribution, not forced sales. The system collateral ratio remains at 3.26 before and after the shock because no trove reaches the minimum collateral ratio on the ruled grid; the first liquidation occurs only at an ETH shock of -80.37%. Consequently, bad debt is $0 and the share of supply represented by bad debt is 0.\n\nThe Stability Pool balance available to absorb liquidations in this scenario is $6.6M, which is the pool balance less the liquidity-provider flight share. No collateral must be sold because LUSD is exempt from the sell-side bound on the absorption path. The exit liquidity in this scenario is $8.8M, and the ratio of forced sales to exit liquidity is 0.\n\nThe system remains structurally insulated; exposure occurs through exit venues only. Liquity v1 is wound down to 68 troves, and recovery mode activates at a TCR drop from 6.5243 to 1.5.",
